Description: fix an out-of-bounds read, enable V-Sync and quit on window close
 show() indexes A[] with acos(cos(P) * cos(T)) / pia, which goes up to 2 * N
 while A[] only had N entries: random memory was read (AddressSanitizer
 reports a global-buffer-overflow). The interference pattern is symmetric,
 A(pi - a) = A(a), so the table is simply computed over [0, pi].
 Also: cast before shifting the alpha value by 24 bits (signed overflow),
 ask sdl12-compat to sync to vblank (the animation advances per frame),
 set a window title, quit on SDL_QUIT and call SDL_Quit().
Author: Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>
Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-20
